<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48038" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Teucer</span></b> , cri (nom.
		Teucrus, <i><span class="en">Verg.
			A. 3, 108</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 21, 1</span></i>),
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τεῦκρος.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Son of Telamon</i>, <i>king of
			Salamis</i>, <i>and brother of Ajax</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				7, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 7, 27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 15, 24</span></i>; 4,
			9, 17; <i><span class="en">id. S. 2, 3, 204</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13,
				157</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 698</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Auct.
				Her. 1, 11, 18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Son of Scamander of Crete</i>, <i>son-in-law of Dardanus</i>, <i>and afterwards
				king of Troy</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13, 705</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 3,
				108</span></i>. — Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Teu-crus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Teu cer;</i>
			<b>poet.</b> transf. for <i>Trojan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					14, 72</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					64, 345</span></i>
			.—As <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Teucri</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				Trojans</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1, 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1,
			248</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 252</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13,
				705</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 728 al.</span></i>; <i>the
			Romans</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 17, 348</span></i>. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Teu-crĭus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Trojan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">moenia,</span>”
				<i>of Troy</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					13, 36</span></i>
			. — Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Teucrĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the Trojan
			country</i>, <i>Troy</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 2,
				26</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Teucris</span></b> ,
			ĭdis, f.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b>
			<i>A Trojan female.</i> captivae, Sabin. 1,
			81.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>A pseudonymic designation of some person</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Teucris illa lentum sane negotium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 1, 12, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 13, 6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
